<h2>3.2. Probabilistic Calibration and Model Reliability</h2>
<p>Clinical integration of AI requires models to output probabilities that genuinely reflect the likelihood of disease, rather than exhibiting overconfidence. We assessed this using the Brier Score and Expected Calibration Error (ECE) (<strong>Table 2</strong>). The MAE-TinyTransformer3D and SwinUNETR-LP models demonstrated exemplary probabilistic reliability (Brier scores of 0.194 and 0.207, respectively). This confirms that the linear-probing and self-supervised approaches not only improve discrimination but also prevent the severe overconfidence typically observed in fully fine-tuned deep neural networks.</p>
